// The World domain: seams on the functions that load and unload the world.
//
// One row per seam, as WXL_SEAM(domain, name, symbol, params):
//
//   domain  the table this row belongs to; the first half of the point's name
//   name    the client function the seam attaches to, never what it means: the second half of
//           the point's name ("World.Preload"), the C++ namespace of its Before and After
//           (wxl::seam::World::Preload), and part of the ABI -- appended, never renamed or
//           dropped
//   symbol  the function's qualified name as the recompiled client spells it: what WXL_SITE
//           resolves on x86, and where the x64 call sites belong
//   params  the parameter list, in parentheses, as the C boundary sees the function's
//           arguments: a reference is a pointer, a class is its SDK struct. Before and After
//           take exactly these; the x86 detour has this signature
//
// A seam is followed by one WXL_SEAM_RAISES(domain, name, event) per event of the contract its
// body raises, naming the event without its WXL_EV_ prefix. Both attachments publish the union as
// the events this runtime can raise, and core/tools/seams/check_seams.py checks each one against
// the body that is supposed to raise it.
//
